{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1134197-pantheons-i-could-use-help-researching","id":1134197,"title":"Pantheons I could use help researching","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-26T11:25:25-07:00","id":1134197,"title":"Pantheons I could use help researching","content":"I've done a lot of research on as many world pantheons as I could for the UDL, but some have proven troublesome in terms of finding specific information to include them. If anyone knows any sources or had knowledge on any of the following pantheons, I would really appreciate it!<br /> <br /> Akamba<br /> Akan<br /> Baluba<br /> Blackfoot<br /> Bushongo<br /> Chilota<br /> Cree<br /> Crow<br /> Dine Bahane<br /> Dravidian<br /> Edo<br /> Efik<br /> Hausa<br /> Ho-Chunk<br /> Hungarian<br /> Hurrian<br /> Isoko<br /> Kaftar<br /> Kallenjin<br /> Kaluli<br /> Kwakwaka'wakw<br /> Leni Lenpae<br /> Lotuko<br /> Lozi<br /> Lugbara<br /> Lummi<br /> Lusitanian<br /> Mangarevean<br /> Melanesian<br /> Micronesian<br /> Miwok<br /> Nuu-chah-nulth<br /> Ohlone<br /> Papuan<br /> Pomo<br /> Rapa Nui<br /> Romani<br /> Ryukyuan<br /> Salish<br /> San<br /> Seneca<br /> Serer<br /> Anything Siberian<br /> Somali<br /> Tahitian<br /> Tongan<br /> Tsimshian<br /> Tumbuka<br /> Tuvaluan<br /> Ute<br /> Vainakh<br /> Waaq<br /> Wyandot<br /> Zuni<br /> <br /> These pantheons have proven particularly troublesome in terms of finding good information. Any help would be greatly appreciated!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T00:50:33-07:00","id":1134391,"title":"","content":"<b>Akan=Ashanti:</b> Check out anything by R. S. Rattray, especially his <i>Akan-Ashanti Folk-Tales</i>. When we get our Ashanti pantheon out, you can look at things more closely there.<br /> <b>Dine Bahane=Navajo:</b> Actually lots of materials there. You can start here: <a href=\"http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/nav/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/nav/index.htm</a> , but the best translation of their myth cycle, I think, is the one by Paul Zolbrod.<br /> <b>Dravidian:</b> Not a culture, but a huge language group in Southern India. Try stuff like <i>Handbook of Hindu Gods, Goddesses and Saints Popular in Contemporary South India</i> by Harry Daniel Smith and <i>Tamil Temple Myths</i> by David Shulman to get started.<br /> <b>Hurrian:</b> Not a lot left, better integrated into Hittite mythology like we did on the Hittite pantheon you'll get to see at ... some point. A complete translation of their myths is included in <i>Hittite Myths</i> by Harry A. Hoffner<br /> <b>Micronesian:</b> There are a lot of histories of Pohnpei in particular, I would poke at that. Otherwise, <i>Summoning the Powers Beyond </i>by Jay Dobbin sounds good.<br /> <b>Miwok: </b>This <a href=\"http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/ca/mim/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/ca/mim/index.htm</a> and this <a href=\"http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/ca/dow/index.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sacred-texts.com/nam/ca/dow/index.htm</a><br /> <b>Seneca=Iroquois:</b> I find Dean Snow's <i>The Iroquois</i> to be a conservative, but very good introduction to Iroquoian culture in general. He outlines important myths and gives pointers on where to find collections of them.<br /> <b>Wyandot:</b> Um, I'll ask Watcher, he should have a thing or two on them.<br /> <br /> <b>various Polynesian cultures: </b>I'm just copying what I have from a bibliography I once started on Polynesia, and never finished. Sorry, Samoa and Tonga are not yet included.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Reading List:</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>General:</u></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Craig, Robert D.: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Handbook of Polynesian Mythology</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. Santa Barbara e.a. 2004.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Craig, Robert D.: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Dictionary of Polynesian Mythology</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. New York 1989.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hiroa, Te Rangi: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Vikings of the Sunrise</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. Christchurch e.a. 1938.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alpers, Antony: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Legends of the South Sea. The World of the Polynesians Seen Through Their Myths and Legends, Poetry and Art</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. London 1970.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Handy, E. S. Craighill: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Polynesian Religion</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. New York 1971.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Poignant, Roslyn: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Oceanic Mythology. The Myths of Polynesia, Micronesia, Melanesia, Australia</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. ??? 1967.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sinclair, Marjorie (ed.): </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Path of Ocean. Traditional Poetry of Polynesia</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. Honolulu 1982.</span></span></li> <li>Luomala, Katharine: <i>Voices on the Wind. Polynesian Chants and Myths</i>. Honolulu 1955.</li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Kirch, Patrick Vinton: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>On the Road of the Winds. An Archaeological History of the Pacific Islands before European Contact</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. Berkeley 2000.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Swain, Tony / Trompf, Garry: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>The Religions of Oceania</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">. London e.a. 1995.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scheffrahn, Wolfgang: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Tangaroa. Ein Beitrag zur polynesischen Religionsgeschichte.</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> T\u00fcbingen 1965.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Luomala, Katharine: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Maui-of-a-Thousand-Tricks</i></span></span><span style=